Subject: GTK: Phoenix build configuration: OpenSSL digests, static libwebkit2gtk, WTF sources, multi-call executable

The PORT=GTK counterpart of the webkit_wpe patches 0006 and 0008, whose PlatformWPE.cmake /
OptionsWPE.cmake hunks the GTK tarball does not have (build-gtk.sh applies the shared patches
with those paths excluded). OptionsGTK.cmake requires libgcrypt and libtasn1: on Phoenix use
OpenSSL, already linked for glib-networking (USE_OPENSSL, PAL's CryptoDigestOpenSSL.cpp,
WebCore's platform/OpenSSL.cmake). libwebkit2gtk is STATIC and JavaScriptCore an OBJECT library
(no shared libraries on Phoenix; GTK makes JSC a shared libjavascriptcoregtk). WTF uses
phoenix/MemoryFootprintPhoenix.cpp (patch 0003) and MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp (patch 0008)
instead of the generic stubs. No translations (no message catalogs on Phoenix, and no
gettext tools needed on the build host). WPE_PHOENIX_DEFAULT_EXECUTABLE (patch 0007's ProcessExecutablePath)
is the GTK browser's install path, /usr/bin/webkit-browser.

diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformGTK.cmake b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformGTK.cmake
index 137aacb3..a2263dd0 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformGTK.cmake
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformGTK.cmake
@@ -68,6 +68,14 @@ if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux")
         linux/MemoryFootprintLinux.cpp
         linux/RealTimeThreads.cpp
 
+        unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp
+    )
+elseif (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Phoenix")
+    # Phoenix-RTOS: no /proc; the footprint comes from meminfo() (patch 0003), the pressure
+    # handler is the Unix one with an OS(PHOENIX) processMemoryUsage() (patch 0008)
+    list(APPEND WTF_SOURCES
+        phoenix/MemoryFootprintPhoenix.cpp
+
         unix/MemoryPressureHandlerUnix.cpp
     )
 elseif (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "FreeBSD" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "QNX")
